cellSysCacheMount: OK_RELAYED keeps the cache for the same id after a session that ended; anything else clears it (OK_CLEARED).

Idea from Re-TeRo17/ps3recomp 8acdefdae7ede7ccecd4db4285985661ea2faf0b "cellSysCacheMount clears the cache it says it
cleared" (MIT); a hand rewrite with a different rule (they clear at every mount), nothing copied.

Problem: Mount always answered CELL_OK (= CELL_SYSCACHE_RET_OK_CLEARED, "the system wiped the cache, start it anew") and
kept every file under PS3_HDD1_ROOT/cache/<id>, and it never removed the cache of another id. A title then trusts a
"fresh" cache that holds whatever an earlier run left, often a run that was killed mid-write (every Proton test run ends
that way). Their report: Drakengard 3's FIOS index left without its header by a killed run made every later start re-read
it 512 bytes at a time (312,000 opens, never reaching the hub). ToD and A4O import cellSysCacheMount; ToD's FIOS keeps
its disc cache there (/dev_hdd1/cache/BCUS98127/cache.idx, the RE notes s.FIOS, port/rc/tests/fios_index_check.py).
Also: an id with '/' or ".." made a host directory outside the cache (cache/../x).

Fix (libs/system/cellSysutil.c, cellSysutil.h):
- One cache: PS3_HDD1_ROOT/cache holds at most the last mounted cache directory.
- Same non-empty id, its directory present, and the last session that mounted a cache ended: OK_RELAYED (1), files kept.
  Otherwise (another id, empty id, no cache yet, or an unfinished session): every entry under PS3_HDD1_ROOT/cache is
  deleted, the new directory created, OK_CLEARED (0).
- "Unfinished session": a mount writes PS3_HDD1_ROOT + ".syscache-open" (outside the guest-visible tree); an atexit
  handler removes it at a normal end of the process (return from main, exit(); the host quit path ends with exit(0)).
  A killed run leaves it and the next mount clears.
- Cache ids are checked against the sysutil name-string rule (A-Z 0-9 '-' '_', not starting with '_'):
  otherwise CELL_SYSCACHE_ERROR_PARAM (0x8002bc03), nothing created.
- No PS3_HDD1_ROOT: unchanged, OK_CLEARED, nothing on the host.
- getCachePath is unchanged (/dev_hdd1/cache/<id>; RPCS3 returns /dev_hdd1 and mounts the cache there: a separate change).
- cellSysCacheClear is unchanged (it still only forgets the mount; RPCS3 empties the cache, keeps it mounted and answers
  OK_CLEARED; ToD calls it from its StageCore boot function after the mount thread, 0x392298): a separate change.

Semantics: RPCS3 cellSysCache.cpp (read 2026-11-19 for behaviour, nothing copied) [src:rpcs3-cellsyscache]: a mount with
a non-empty id equal to the current cache id answers OK_RELAYED; otherwise the previous cache is removed, the new one
created (emptied if it was there) and OK_CLEARED; a mounted cache is marked incomplete and a marked cache is never
reused; ids are checked with sysutil_check_name_string. RPCS3 also deletes the cache at a normal stop unless it saves
state, so on RPCS3 the first mount of a boot is always OK_CLEARED; here a cache from a session that ended is relayed.
ASSUMPTION: the console keeps the system cache across boots of the same title (what OK_RELAYED and the XMB's
"delete system cache" boot option are for).

Tests: libs/system/tests/test_syscache_mount.c (tools/test_syscache_mount.py; R&C runner
port/rc/tests/run_syscache_mount_test.sh): seven sessions as forked children (_exit = killed): first mount CLEARED +
path + dir; same id same session RELAYED, file kept; same id next session RELAYED, file kept; another id CLEARED, old
cache gone; back CLEARED, other gone; after a killed session CLEARED and empty; empty id CLEARED twice; '../x' and '_LEAD'
PARAM, nothing outside the cache; no root CLEARED. 22 checks PASS. Negative control (cellSysutil.c without this patch):
FAIL, 10 of 22 (no RELAYED, old caches kept, files of a killed session kept, '../x' accepted and cache/../x created).
